     "label": "Tens",
     "value": 2
    },
    {
     "label": "Ones",
     "value": 5
    }
   ],
   "caption": "Read the digits: four thousand, eight hundred and twenty-five."
  },
  {
   "type": "check",
   "question": {
    "type": "number",
    "prompt": "What is the value of the 7 in 3,742?",
    "hint": "Which column is the 7 in?",
    "answer": {
     "value": 700,
     "tolerance": 0
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "markdown": "We can **round** a number to make it easier to work with. 3,742 is nearer to 3,700 than 3,800, so it rounds to 3,700.\n\nRounding also helps us **estimate**: 398 + 402 is about 400 + 400 = 800."
  },
  {
   "type": "chart",
   "kind": "number_line",
   "title": "Is 42 nearer to 0 or to 100?",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 100,
   "step": 10,
   "marks": [
    0,
    42,
    100
   ],
   "caption": "The last two digits of 3,742 are 42. That is nearer to 0, so we round down to 3,700."
  },
  {
   "type": "check",
   "question": {
    "type": "number",
    "prompt": "Round 3,742 to the nearest hundred.",
    "hint": "Is the tens digit 5 or more?",
    "answer": {
     "value": 3700,
     "tolerance": 0
    }
   }
  },
